    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW23YPHZgtrQdmM3x3d757z7z)_\n\n## Summary\n\n- **Problem (comment on #487):** `d` (drop) in the author works report gets slow and the buffer hangs. `u` restore and `g` refresh took the same path.\n- **Cause:** `d`, `u` and `g` draw the whole report again through `sp-batch-report-open`, which called the mode function every time. That re-runs `org-mode` over the whole old buffer: all of `org-mode-hook` (`org-indent-mode`, `org-num-mode`, `org-table-widget-mode`, cite hover, ...), reset of buffer state, then the buffer is erased and filled. Before #492 the table widget also laid out every table again on each of those.\n- **Fix:** `sp-batch-report-open` starts the mode only when the buffer is not in it yet. Same for every other report that uses it (litnote titles, tag lint, footnote lint, normalise, notes filing ...). The buffer-local state is set afterwards as before.\n- Also: a table cell is only escaped when it holds `|` or a newline (the common case did two regexp passes per cell).\n- **Not done, on purpose:** editing only the affected row and table in place. After this change the redraw is a plain text rebuild; a local edit would be a larger change and a new UI that renders reports as a `vulpea-ui-schema-dashboard` style special-mode buffer is being worked on in another thread, which may replace this Org renderer and supersede this PR.\n- Docs are bullet lists (`sp-batch-report.org`); `.el` matches. `when-let*` only; no CHANGELOG edit.\n\n## Timings (Emacs 29.3 batch, synthetic data, byte-compiled code, `org-indent-mode` and `org-num-mode` in `org-mode-hook`; one drop = `sp-batch-report-drop` + redisplay + font-lock of the first 20k characters)\n\n| Report size | Drop before | Drop after |\n|---|---|---|\n| 100 tables, 1000 rows | 0.04 to 0.11 s | 0.02 to 0.07 s |\n| 300 tables, 6000 rows | 0.34 to 0.49 s | 0.11 to 0.27 s |\n| 300 tables, restore | 0.42 s | 0.35 s |\n| 120 tables with the table widget **on** (`sp-batch-report-table-widgets` t) | 3.4 to 4.3 s | 1.4 to 1.6 s |\n\n- With your real hooks (org-modern, vulpea, cite hover, ...) the avoided mode run costs more than in these runs, but I could not measure that: no access to your machine. Please time a drop on your side.\n- The text rebuild is now the bulk of what is left (about 0.1 s for 6000 rows compiled).\n- **Tests:** `sp-batch-report-test` 24 pass (1 new: the mode and its hook run once for several draws, a different `:mode` still starts), `sp-author-notes-bibtex-test` 16 pass.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [x] `cd ~/dotfiles; git fetch origin 494-batch-report-fast-redraw; git checkout 494-batch-report-fast-redraw`, restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`)\n- [x] `M-x sp-author-notes-bibtex`; press `d` on several entries one after another: each drop is quick, no hang, point stays on the same line\n- [x] `u` on a dropped entry, and `g`: both quick; dropped entries stay dropped after `g`\n- [x] Drop 20 or more entries: the time per drop does not grow\n- [x] Another report (`M-x sp-litnotes-titles-dryrun` or the tag lint): `d`, `u`, `g`, `A` still work and the hints stay in the echo area\n- [ ] A report that opens in its own mode (footnote lint, tag lint `a` key) still has its keys after a redraw\n- [ ] Optional: `M-x profiler-start`, drop an entry, `M-x profiler-report`, and send me the top entries if it is still slow\n\n<details><summary>Revert after testing</summary>\n\n- Discard local edits: `git -C ~/dotfiles status`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles restore .`\n- Back to main: `git -C ~/dotfiles switch main`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles pull`\n- Optionally `git -C ~/dotfiles branch -D 494-batch-report-fast-redraw`\n- Restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`)\n\n</details>\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiAF6gJZsaMTJLEA9cM)_",
